In the misty solitude of the shower, the disciple enters a state of transcendence. The warm waters wash away the foolishness of the world, purifying not just the body, but the mind. Here, within the blessed downpour, one is reborn\emdash 
not as a participant in pointless disputes, but as a free entity, unshackled by nonsense.
\par Meanwhile, the one left behind, expecting a battle of words, is now trapped in their own bewilderment.
\par \'93Where did he go?\'94
\par \'93Did I\'85 did I just lose?\'94
\par \'93What kind of sorcery is this?\'94
\par And thus, the battle is won not through conflict, but through disappearance.
