{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9075342 
The Absurdist does not waste his days hammering at the walls of the unwilling. Instead, he walks freely, dancing on the open plains of uncertainty, laughing in the face of rigid minds. He does not seek to tear down cages\emdash 
he simply refuses to live in one. And occasionally, he throws peanuts at the Keepers of the Cage just to see if they react.
\par And should a prisoner one day peer beyond their bars and ask,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\cf1\dbch\af31501\insrsid9075342 \~}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\i\cf1\dbch\af31501\insrsid9075342 \loch\af0\dbch\af31501\hich\f0 \'93\loch\f0 
\hich\f0 What is out there?\'94}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9075342 \emdash the Absurdist will welcome them with open arms. Until then, he lets them be.
\par For the greatest freedom is knowing when to walk away. And when to stop offering unsolicited wisdom\emdash unless it involves snacks.
