{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid7697771 One day, Jesus came strolling through the land of the Keepers of the Cage. They saw him and gasped, for he was not bound by their walls.
\par \'93Who are you, that you walk so freely?\'94 they demanded.
\par \'93I am,\'94 Jesus replied, unhelpfully.
\par The Keepers blinked. \'93You must obey the rules!\'94 they insisted. \'93Where is your cage?!\'94
\par Jesus picked up a stone and held it out to them. \'93If a man believes this is bread, and eats it, will he not be full?\'94
\par The Keepers murmured among themselves. \'93No,\'94 they said. \'93He will be a fool.\'94
\par Jesus nodded. \'93And if a man believes his cage is freedom, is he not the same?\'94
\par At this, the Absurdist grinned and handed Jesus a banana. Jesus took it, peeled it with divine grace, and took a bite. The Keepers gasped again.
\par \'93Blasphemy!\'94 one shouted. \'93That is not a proper meal!\'94
\par Jesus shrugged. \'93Man shall not live by bread alone.\'94 Then, with a wink, he added, \'93Sometimes, a banana is enough.\'94
\par The Absurdist cheered. The Keepers, confused and horrified, returned to fortifying their walls.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s37\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6757355 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid7697771 
