{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9900580 One day, Jesus returned, strolling once more through the land of the Keepers of the Cage.
\par They gasped. \'93Lord! You have come back! You will surely bless us, for we have followed your teachings!\'94
\par Jesus blinked. \'93You have?\'94 He looked around. \'93I don\rquote t remember telling anyone to build all these cages.\'94
\par The Keepers straightened their robes. \'93But Lord, we have maintained order. We have rules. We have identified the righteous and condemned the sinners. We have kept the faith exactly as we were taught!\'94
\par Jesus sighed. \'93And you\rquote ve also built walls around yourselves so high that no joy, no love, no laughter can get in.\'94 He shook his head. \'93You\rquote ve become the very Pharisees I warned you about.\'94
\par The Keepers gasped in horror. \'93Impossible! We are your truest followers!\'94
\par Jesus raised an eyebrow. \'93Then why am I having a better time with the absurdists over there?\'94 He pointed to a group of people in the distance, juggling fish, turning water into wine just for fun, and taking turns riding a donkey in a silly hat.

\par The Keepers scowled. \'93They are fools! They do not follow the sacred rules!\'94
\par Jesus grinned. \'93Exactly.\'94
