\par One of the Keepers, adjusting their glasses, clears their throat. "Actually, according to these 300 pages, love can only exist if we adhere to a strict set of conditions, particularly when it concerns... uh, the color of robes during communion and the pro
per number of loaves of bread per person."
\par Jesus\rquote s eyes narrow as he stares at them, blinking slowly. "Is it really love if it requires so many footnotes? Are we really talking about love, or a corporate policy?"
\par The Keepers look at each other. "Hmm... Good question. Maybe love is... a policy with a few exceptions."
\par Jesus throws his hands up. "No, it's not! Love is supposed to be free, unconditional, spontaneous! Not... another contract!" He looks to the sky, wondering if maybe a giant butterfly might swoop in to interrupt this nonsense.
\par But no butterfly. Just more rules. And more essays.
\par Jesus sighs again. "Maybe I\rquote ll try explaining this on TikTok."
